      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "How stale an event was when the VENDOR accepted it, not how long the HTTP call took. A destination whose vendor answers in 40ms while its consumer sits an hour behind looks perfectly healthy on the duration panels \u2014 the lag is upstream of the only thing they measure. Measured from occurred_at (the producer's clock), because the question is how stale the vendor's picture of this customer is, and the customer acted at occurred_at.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
